00: "org0001:100000" (100000-1005F4)


Source: "/home/ryan/Code/AtariST/gamebench/games/in_progress/moonshine-racers/work/campfloppy/campread2.s"
                            	     1: ; campread.s -- SCRATCH PROTOTYPE (MSRCampFloppy): read MSTRACKS.TRK from a FAT12 floppy with the floppy game's OWN FDC
                            	     2: ; swap prompts.  Assembled at ORG = $100000 and loaded into a running game with the Hatari debugger (work/campfloppy/*.
                            	     3: ;
                            	     4: ; camp_read   in:  d0.w = unit (0 = drive A, 1 = drive B), a0 = destination (even, DMA range < $400000), d1.l = max fil
                            	     5: ;             out: d0.w = status, d1.l = file size
                            	     6: ;   0 ok | 1 no disk in the drive (no index pulse) | 2 read error | 3 not a FAT floppy this driver reads | 4 no MSTRACK
                            	     7: ;   5 file larger than max | 6 not a campaign file (magic 'MSTK', count 1..15, header length = file size)
                            	     8: ; The geometry comes from the disk's BPB (sectors per track 9..11): the game's driver takes the track length from the H
                            	     9: ; 720 KB TOS disk that msrtrack.py makes is read as it is.  FAT chain is NOT followed: the file must be contiguous (the
                            	    10: ORG     equ     $100000
                            	    11:         org     ORG
                            	    12: 
